WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.040
- You had a home birth for
your second baby, right?

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:04.660
- For Banks, yeah and for Mae.

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:05.990
- So for your second and third?

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:07.045
- Yes.

00:00:07.045 --> 00:00:07.878
- Was that, I mean, was that like a

00:00:07.878 --> 00:00:09.330
cause you had your first
one in the hospital.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:10.163
- Yup.

00:00:10.163 --> 00:00:11.240
- And you had a fine experience probably,

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:13.180
but what was the reason why'd
you wanna do home birth?

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:16.280
cause it kind of terrifies
me cause I had complications.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:18.280
So you never know when you're
gonna have complications.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:19.760
- Yeah, yeah, Well, you know what?

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.550
I think that I had a really
easy first birth with Luca

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:24.720
in the hospital, so I was
kind of like, all right

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:25.930
I know my body can do this.

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:26.763
I didn't have any issues.

00:00:26.763 --> 00:00:28.008
- Great body, okay, yeah.

00:00:28.008 --> 00:00:29.299
(audience laughter)

00:00:29.299 --> 00:00:31.380
- My body was not that body.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:32.213
- You know what?

00:00:32.213 --> 00:00:33.580
Some people like aren't,
birthers like that.

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:34.780
- Yeah, my sister's like you.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:36.370
- My mom was like you.

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:37.600
So it's weird.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.570
I was very like, much
more comfortable doing it

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:41.080
in the hospital for the first time.

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:43.600
And then I watched Ricky Lake's business

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:46.930
of being born and I was like,
I think I could do this.

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:47.763
I think I can.

00:00:47.763 --> 00:00:48.596
- Wait. I missed that.

00:00:48.596 --> 00:00:50.353
So wait, it was just
like a home birth movie?

00:00:50.353 --> 00:00:51.555
- It's a home birth documentary.

00:00:51.555 --> 00:00:52.707
- Oh, I missed that.

00:00:52.707 --> 00:00:54.780
- You know what was really cool
about the home birth Kelly?

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:57.200
It's like, you know,
you're bringing a baby

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.033
into the world,

00:00:58.033 --> 00:00:59.860
that's some of the hardest
work anybody can do.

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:00.693
- Amen.

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:03.410
- And they don't let you have
like water in the hospital

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:04.670
or food or snacks.

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:06.300
And you're about to like work the hardest

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.480
you've ever worked to
like push a baby out.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:09.650
- So at home you get all?

00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:11.720
- Oh, I had sugar fish in bed.

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:13.019
I had a glass of rose.

00:01:13.019 --> 00:01:13.852
- You had sushi?

00:01:13.852 --> 00:01:17.130
- I had sushi in my bed
with my baby and a glass

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:20.500
of rose that I actually was
like clawing at the bit to have.

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:22.370
And then I took a sip
afterwards and I was like

00:01:22.370 --> 00:01:23.370
it's not doing it for me.

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:24.203
- Yeah.

00:01:24.203 --> 00:01:25.760
- But the day after I had some.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:27.010
- That's amazing I'm so glad.

00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:28.340
That's such a cool experience too

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:29.650
for like your kids when they grow up

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:30.860
it's like you are born at home.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:31.693
That's so special.

00:01:31.693 --> 00:01:32.852
- You know what?

00:01:32.852 --> 00:01:34.510
It's kind of the most
hippy dippy thing about me.

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:37.600
Like to have like my kids
around while I'm birthing.

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:39.700
At first I thought it was
really weird, but it was really

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:42.403
beautiful to like bring
another family member

00:01:42.403 --> 00:01:43.820
in with everyone else.

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:44.760
- I don't think it's very hippie dippie,

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:46.640
but I think it's self-sustaining, it's

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:48.100
like you can do everything at your home.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:49.020
I think that's awesome.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:50.419
- You know what?

00:01:50.419 --> 00:01:52.110
One of my favorite memories
was like Luca decided to

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:54.270
sing Mae happy birthday.

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:56.100
And I was like, I've never
heard of anyone singing

00:01:56.100 --> 00:02:00.530
happy birthday on a like
entering date, but he was like

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:02.133
we should sing a happy birthday.

00:02:03.366 --> 00:02:04.793
- I think that's so precious.

